QUALIFY VERDICT 2026-07-27: NOT yet qualified for heavy sustained write.
- W-read (catalog zero-page): VERIFIED FIXED (535791372) - 24 concurrent cold-catalog readers x3 = OK=24 FAIL=0.
- W-arcwrite + W-lfmutex: SAME root cause = taskq_wait 8-worker barrier bug. FIXED (taskqueue_drain_all, 51c147066 on #1423). Moved pgbench -i -s1000 from crash@27% to complete-at-large-RAM.
- WALL 3 (OPEN): 2nd distinct bug - ZFS write-pipeline object-lifetime corruption in txg_sync/zio-completion under sustained write. Racy + memory-pressure-sensitive. 5 gdb signatures (db_buf==NULL, dbuf parent UAF, range-tree btree corruption, range-tree bounds corruption, preemptable()/mempool::free completion-free-on-COW-page). NOT a missing identity-heap wrapper (all ZFS allocs audited). Smoking gun = signature (e): cross-AS coherence gap in the OSv per-CPU MEMPOOL MAGAZINE/SLAB a forked backend refilled, hit on the completion free path. Tag [fork-stack/CONF_fork].
- Survives (with taskq fix): s100/s500 clean; s1000 completes @96GB RAM OR recordsize=32k@32GB; -c16 -T120 = 304,639 txns 0-failed then eventually corrupts. recordsize=32k + RAM = mitigations NOT fixes.
- NEXT to close Wall 3: instrument mempool::free/fork-arena to log faulting VA + owning AS on a COW-page completion free at full speed (gdb hides the race), then extend identity-heap coverage to the per-CPU mempool magazine/slab.
